{"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"title":"Explanation"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Core Middleware","type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","level":3,"text":"Importing at call sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"separate library target"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ui(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The easy case to forget is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The fix is to add ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to that file.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Comparison","anchor":"Comparison","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Target"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Capture state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"flush() async","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Registration-Order","level":2,"text":"Registration Order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}]},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"service-result action","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Do ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"state slice","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2,"text":"Next Steps","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle.","type":"text"}],"title":"PluginHost","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Undo \/ Redo","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"abstract":[{"text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes.","type":"text"}],"title":"Persistence Middleware","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"title":"Architecture & Performance","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"kind":"article","title":"Design Principles","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"title":"Store","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}]}}}